From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 12:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm4450: Set HW_CTRL_TRIGGER for video GDSC

The iris video driver uses dev_pm_genpd_set_hwmode() to switch the
vcodec0 GDSC between HW and SW control at runtime, which needs the
domain to have HW_CTRL_TRIGGER. HW_CTRL instead puts it in HW mode for
good at every enable, and genpd then refuses the switch, so iris could
not start its core.

The same change upstream made for gcc-sm6115 (ab171a6afd4e) and
gcc-qcm2290 (972380704660), which share the SM4450's AR50_LITE core.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm4450.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm4450.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm4450.c
index 2001ed54c9c5..16fda714eac4 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm4450.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm4450.c
@@ -2591,7 +2591,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_vcodec0_gdsc = {
 		.name = "gcc_vcodec0_gdsc",
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | HW_CTRL,
+	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc gcc_venus_gdsc = {
-- 
2.47.0

